0019A0  1               ;
0019A0  1               ; "STRLT2" TAKES THE STRING LITERAL WHOSE FIRST CHARACTER
0019A0  1               ; IS POINTED TO BY [Y,A] AND BUILDS A DESCRIPTOR FOR IT.
0019A0  1               ; THE DESCRIPTOR IS INITIALLY BUILT IN "DSCTMP", BUT "PUTNEW"
0019A0  1               ; TRANSFERS IT INTO A TEMPORARY AND LEAVES A POINTER
0019A0  1               ; AT THE TEMPORARY IN FACMO&LO. THE CHARACTERS OTHER THAN
0019A0  1               ; ZERO THAT TERMINATE THE STRING SHOULD BE SET UP IN "CHARAC"
0019A0  1               ; AND "ENDCHR". IF THE TERMINATOR IS A QUOTE, THE QUOTE IS SKIPPED
0019A0  1               ; OVER. LEADING QUOTES SHOULD BE SKIPPED BEFORE JSR. ON RETURN
0019A0  1               ; THE CHARACTER AFTER THE STRING LITERAL IS POINTED TO
0019A0  1               ; BY [STRNG2].
0019A0  1               ;
